```
-run regexp
    if specified, only runs generate directives that match the regexp
```

Implementation: for each directive line, it splits by fields and checks if regexp matches any field... Let me recall go/build generate.go:

```go
if *run != "" {
    for _, word := range words {
        if re.MatchString(word) {
            match = true
        }
    }
}
```
Hmm, actually:
```go
// Check for run match
if gen.run != nil {
    match := false
    for _, word := range words {
        if gen.run.MatchString(word) {
            match = true
            break
        }
    }
    if !match { continue }
