```
Yes, it matches against each whitespace-separated field. So `-run 'genstub'` would match the field "./internal/genstub". And would it match "go run ./internal/preflight"? Fields: "go", "run", "./internal/preflight" — no "genstub" field. Good.

To be safe, use `-run '^genstub$'`? No — fields include "./internal/genstub", so `^genstub$` wouldn't match. Use `-run 'genstub'`. That's precise enough given only two directives.

